What:   restoring the cursor (DECRC, ESC 8) keeps a pending wrap. restore_cursor clamped the
        column to size.cols - 1, but size.cols is where the cursor waits after writing to the
        last column; clamping it made the next character overwrite the last one of the row
        instead of starting the next row (lost input on screen). It also broke restoring such
        a screen on reattach, since contents_formatted encodes a pending wrap with DECSC/DECRC.
        Only a column beyond size.cols (the screen shrank after the save) is clamped now.
        Fixes el, il_dl and relative_movement in tests/csi.rs, failing since the clamp came in
        (1348bec), so shpool_vt100's whole suite passes.
Where:  src/grid.rs (restore_cursor), tests/escape.rs (two tests).
Shape:  fixes behaviour.
Needs:  01-last-n-rows.patch before it (cut against its result; they share no lines).
Status: offered upstream on branch wmacevoy/shpool_vt100:fix/restore-cursor-pending-wrap
        (PR to shell-pool/shpool_vt100 not yet opened).

diff --git a/src/grid.rs b/src/grid.rs
